{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs Java 6 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following Java 6 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nLittle Petya loves training spiders. Petya has a board n\u2009\u00d7\u2009m in size. Each cell of the board initially has a spider sitting on it. After one second Petya chooses a certain action for each spider, and all of them humbly perform its commands. There are 5 possible commands: to stay idle or to move from current cell to some of the four side-neighboring cells (that is, one command for each of the four possible directions). Petya gives the commands so that no spider leaves the field. It is allowed for spiders to pass through each other when they crawl towards each other in opposite directions. All spiders crawl simultaneously and several spiders may end up in one cell. Petya wants to know the maximum possible number of spider-free cells after one second.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the Java 6 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n        try {\n            File f = new File(\"input.txt\");\n            if (f.exists()) {\n                System.setIn(new FileInputStream(f));\n            }\n        } catch (SecurityException e) {\n        }\n\n        Thread t = new Thread(null, new Runnable() {\n            public void run() {\n                try {\n                    new Main().start();\n                } catch (Exception e) {\n                    e.printStackTrace();\n                    System.exit(999);\n                }\n            }\n        }, \"Main\", 1 << 23);\n        t.start();\n    }\n\n    BufferedReader br;\n    PrintWriter pw;\n    StringTokenizer st = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    int R, C;\n    int[][][] dp;\n    int INF = Integer.MAX_VALUE >> 1;\n    int minUsed = Integer.MAX_VALUE;\n\n    void start() throws Exception {\n        br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        pw = new PrintWriter(System.out);\n\n        R = nextInt();\n        C = nextInt();\n        if (R < C) {\n            int tmp = R;\n            R = C;\n            C = tmp;\n        }\n\n        int M = 1 << C;\n        dp = new int[R][M << 1][M << 1];\n        for (int i = 0; i < R; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < (M << 1); j++) {\n                Arrays.fill(dp[i][j], INF);\n            }\n        }\n\n        dp[0][0][0] = 0;\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < R; i++) {\n            for (int mask1 = 0; mask1 < M; mask1++) {\n                for (int mask2 = 0; mask2 < M; mask2++) {\n                    if (dp[i][mask1][mask2] == INF) continue;\n\n                    for (int nmask1 = 0; nmask1 < M; nmask1++) {\n                        for (int nmask2 = 0; nmask2 < M; nmask2++) {\n                            int covered1 = mask1 | nmask1 | (nmask1 << 1) | (nmask1 >> 1) | nmask2;\n                            covered1 &= (M - 1);\n\n                            if (covered1 != (M - 1)) continue;\n\n                            int covered2 = mask2 | nmask1 | (nmask2 << 1) | (nmask2 >> 1) | nmask2;\n                            covered2 &= (M - 1);\n\n                            int next1 = covered2 & (M - 1);\n                            int next2 = nmask2 & (M - 1);\n                            int cost = Integer.bitCount(nmask1) + Integer.bitCount(nmask2);\n\n                            if (i < R - 1) {\n                                if (dp[i + 1][next1][next2] > dp[i][mask1][mask2] + cost) {\n                                    dp[i + 1][next1][next2] = dp[i][mask1][mask2] + cost;\n                                }\n                            } else {\n                                if ((covered1 & (M - 1)) == (M - 1)) {\n                                    if (dp[i][mask1][mask2] + cost < minUsed) {\n                                        minUsed = dp[i][mask1][mask2] + cost;\n                                    }\n                                }\n                            }\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        pw.println(R * C - minUsed);\n        br.close();\n        pw.close();\n    }\n\n    String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!st.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            st = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());\n        }\n        return st.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    int nextInt() throws IOException {\n        return Integer.parseInt(next());\n    }\n\n    long nextLong() throws IOException {\n        return Long.parseLong(next());\n    }\n\n    double nextDouble() throws IOException {\n        return Double.parseDouble(next());\n    }\n\n    String nextLine() throws IOException {\n        st = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n        return br.readLine();\n    }\n\n    boolean isEOF() throws IOException {\n        while (!st.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            String line = br.readLine();\n            if (line == null) return true;\n            st = new StringTokenizer(line);\n        }\n        return false;\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{